 believe that  with the measures we're now taking  we can do it and then we will need to  defend that success  we need to make sure that it can be  sustained that in conjunction with the  effects of spring in the vaccine  this allows us to return to normality  and that we don't face renewed problems  especially through a highly infectious  virus mutation that is even harder to  control  i believe we all want to avoid that and  that's why stricter immigration measures  when a neighbouring region has become a  host to mutation simply can't be avoided  now the united states has been following  a america first policy also when it  comes to vaccinations that goes back to  a presidential order from the 8th of  december  it makes sure that every american has to  be offered vaccination before  any of these vaccines leave the country  so what will your request be on this  issue  to the newly inaugurated president joe  biden  european commission is currently in  talks with the companies involved  and if that helps us find a solution  then of course we will discuss that with  the us administration  there's no question about that now the  world health organization is criticizing  that it's the rich countries who are  getting access to vaccines  first what are you doing for poorer  countries  just as we ordered the vaccine through  the european union  so too we are taking part in a joint  initiative together with the european  union  the european commission will address  this topic  how to provide the vaccine to  third-party states especially poorer  countries  will be atop at the european council on  thursday  including the question of how we can  still do more  beyond this kovacs initiative  chief of staff for german chancellor  angela marco thank you very much  here's a quick look at some other  developments in the global pandemic  china plans to impose strict coveted  testing requirements during the lunar  new year holiday season  when millions of people are expected to  travel the country is battling the worst  wave of  new infections since last march the  netherlands will ban flights from the uk  south africa and south america beginning  saturday for a month  the country is also set to debate a  nationwide curfew aiming  aimed at curbing infections and  australia has recorded a fourth day of  zero cases this comes a day before new  rules  go into effect requiring international  visitors to test negative for  coronavirus within  72 hours before departure
 

